Bakery Fats and Oils comprise lipid ingredients specifically engineered for baked goods such as bread, cakes, cookies, and laminated pastries. Unlike ordinary edible oils, these fats are optimized for lamination performance, stability, whipping ability, and flavor delivery. The category includes natural milk‑fat products (e.g., butter) and industrially modified vegetable fats (e.g., shortening, margarine, specialized baking fats). In dough systems they contribute both flavor and structure: fats coat flour particles to limit gluten development in cakes and cookies, while in laminated products they create distinct layers that expand as steam during baking.
