What are Bakery Fats and Oils?
Bakery fats and oils are specialized lipid blends that serve three core purposes in baked products: (1) they impart desirable mouthfeel and flavor, (2) they regulate dough rheology to achieve specific textures such as tenderness, flakiness, or lift, and (3) they enhance shelf‑life by acting as barriers to moisture loss and oxidation. Modern formulations often incorporate functional additives-emulsifiers, antioxidants, and enzyme systems-that allow manufacturers to fine‑tune melt points, plasticity, and oxidative stability without compromising clean‑label claims.
